one  and take that extra photo and then merge  them and figure them all out later on  you can take it all on that one device  so that isn't a deal breaker but it is  definitely an added benefit of the s7  now when it comes down to apple we have  a much more even battle on our hands  we have the apple air that has just been  released and redesigned  and the apple ipad pro now both of these  devices are phenomenal  both of them will be able to do the job  unlike the samsung comparison  there isn't unfortunately a medium  competitor that's able  to keep up with the s7 so in the apple  world we have both of these devices  which do fantastic things but there is  some key points that you need to be  aware of  now when selecting a tablet as an  architect you have to keep in mind  what we actually do with a tablet you're  going to be bringing up drawings  bringing up videos bringing up 3ds  and you're going to be taking a lot of  notes you're going to be sketching and  marking up all over drawings  and maybe if you're artistic you're  going to be able to draw and replicate  some beautiful 3d  hand sketch renders so the device has to  be  pretty powerful to be able to run this  the battery has to be pretty good  and in my personal opinion the screen  has to be perfect  because if you're going to look at  something all day you're going to want  the screen to be as best as possible  to make sure that your eyesight stays as  good as possible for as long as possible  so the brand new apple ipad air comes  with the new a14 chip whilst the apple  ipad pro comes with the old  a12 zip between these two the ipad air  is  more powerful than the ipad pro but  overall they're pretty much similar for  what we do you don't need any more  powerful than  these two devices neither one features  fast charging but the ipad air has 20  watt charging versus 18 watt  on the ipad pro the difference comes  down to price and budget the ipad air  costs nine hundred dollars to about  fourteen hundred 